"""Leigh Johnson, part B: Personality (official description, observable traits, In his own words, Names and title,
Appearance), Law enforcement, weapons and horses (the fiche-specific skills section), Relationships
(21 Oct 2026, medium tier).

Coverage: the Red Dead Wiki EN sections Personality and Appearance, the GOTY quote box, the infobox (aka, affiliations,
weapons, mount, family, occupation, location), the trivia items on his badge and jurisdiction, his wife's grave, the
two revolvers used only in cutscenes, the horses, the two-holster gun belt, killing him after "Hanging Bonnie
MacFarlane" and in Undead Nightmare, and the townsfolk who speak ill of him; plus the pages "Jonah", "Eli",
"Priscilla Johnson", "Norman Deek", "Walton Lowe", "Baxter Deaton", "Mel Thaxton", "Jake", "Drew MacFarlane",
"Dinner for Two" and the five RDR1 transcripts. Narrative events are told in part A; entries below point to them.

SOURCE REGISTER (read 21 Oct 2026; wiki cache scripts/v3/work/_m/):
- Official description: Red Dead Redemption: Game of the Year Edition Guide (BradyGames), quoted in the quote box of
  the Red Dead Wiki EN page "Leigh Johnson" ("He is a 50-year-old ageing cynic..."). The guide itself was not read:
  quoted through the wiki, attributed. Rockstar's 6 Sep 2018 descriptions (sources/thr_descriptions.txt) cover the
  RDR2 gang only: none for Johnson.
- Transcripts (every quoted line checked): "Political Realities in Armadillo/dialogues", "Justice in Pike's
  Basin/dialogues", "Spare the Rod, Spoil the Bandit/dialogues", "Hanging Bonnie MacFarlane/dialogues", "The Assault
  on Fort Mercer/dialogues"; "Exodus in America/dialogues" (Jake: "it was the Marshal who hired me. Leigh Johnson");
  "Obstacles in Our Path/dialogues" (Bonnie: "go pay the Marshal a visit in Armadillo"); "Women and Cattle/dialogues"
  (Bonnie heard John's plans "from Leigh Johnson").
- Mission pages: "Dinner for Two" (no transcript exists: Sawed-off Shotgun handed over, one revolver only, the Marshal
  can be killed through the window afterwards), "Political Realities in Armadillo".
- Other wiki pages: "Jonah" (Irish heritage claim, red shirt), "Eli" (lazy eye), "Priscilla Johnson" (grave at
  Coot's Chapel, died April 23, 1903, "Forever Smiling In Our Hearts"), "Norman Deek" (two holsters, quote "You wait,
  Marshal" checked in the transcript), "Walton Lowe" (wiki quote "Whoever kills the Marshal gets to keep the badge!"),
  "Baxter Deaton" (manager of the Bank of Armadillo; quote list incl. "a certain Marshal" and "up at Pleasance House";
  admits most rumors are made up), "Mel Thaxton" (lawman; quote list incl. "This whole organization stinks!"), "Jake"
  (hired guide).
- Newspaper: Blackwater Ledger & Sentinel No. 213 (1914), "Marshall Johnson of Armadillo Retires", read on the page
  image (seth/fc/Blackwater_Ledger_Sentinel_No_213.png): headline "MARSHALL JOHNSON", subhead "Legendary Armadillo
  Marshal", body "town marshal".
- Visual check: the live portrait.jpeg and gallery-1.jpeg for Appearance.

OWNERSHIP NOTES:
- Quoted HERE only (part C must not repeat them): the GOTY description; "Well, I ain't happy, but I also ain't
  suicidal."; "My cause is to keep this town..."; "I remember when we first got here..."; "Killing and thieving's
  never right, boy..."; "Criminals are like weeds..." (In his own words); "Yes, sir, Mr. Johnson, sir", "Oh, Mister
  Marshal", Bonnie's "Yes, from Leigh Johnson." (Names); "I trust you..." (John); "Simmer down, Jonah." (Jonah);
  "Now Drew, nobody's lost anything yet." (Drew); "He's certainly a character, that West Dickens." (Dickens);
  "a glorified errand boy" (Deek); "There's the dumb rat-bastard now.", "Because that ain't how the law works.",
  "And alive, he can still talk." (Walton); Baxter Deaton's and Mel Thaxton's lines (townsfolk).
- Quoted ONLY in C Quotes (paraphrased here, without quotation marks; fixer, 21 Oct 2026): Jake's "Leigh Johnson"
  exchange, "Nor did I, my friend...", "federal clowns", "I'm sorry about this, John.", Deek's "mean enough..." and
  "You wait, Marshal...", the Ridgewood survivor's "government payroll" exchange, "We don't do deals with outlaws,
  boy.", "this country is infested...", "the narcotic and bat piss salesman...", "Ya hear that, Marston?...", "That
  sarcasm's most unbecoming, Eli...", "That man is a stone-cold killer.".
- Fixer decisions (FIX_RULES.md): townsfolk criticism lives here only (Trivia copy cut); the two-holster belt lives in
  Weapons only; the kill tip and the Undead Nightmare office/window kill live in "In the game" only; Priscilla's grave
  is told in A Origins (pointer here); the "Marshall" spelling is in C Trivia only; Armadillo 731 and Jake's hiring
  are in A only. The wiki trivia "Jake says he is not the man he used to be" stays excluded (see below).
- Told once elsewhere, pointer here: every mission event (A); the 1914 retirement party and his plans (A, Epilogue);
  the Liars and Cheats model, "L. Johnson's Run", Red Dead Online mention by Bonnie, RDR2's Sheriff Palmer (C Other
  media / Trivia); the promotional picture with the Campo Mirada bounty (C Trivia); the voice actors (D).
- Gameplay HERE only: dual revolvers in cutscenes only, horses, killing him after "Hanging Bonnie MacFarlane" (wiki
  trivia + Kotaku, Owen Good, 17 Aug 2010) and after "Dinner for Two", the deputies-or-Marshal choice at Pike's Basin.

WIKI-ONLY (kept, attributed): the GOTY guide description; the weapons and the Standardbred Pinto of the infobox; the
Tersk and the Kentucky Saddler (trivia); the dual revolvers only in cutscenes; the yellow tinge of the beard; the
two-holster belt shared with Norman Deek, Enepay and Benton Manning ("Norman Deek" page); the townsfolk's remarks (Baxter Deaton, Mel Thaxton, Jeb Murphy, Eldin
Grubb, Herbert Moon, the MacFarlane's Ranch NPCs); Jonah's Irish-heritage claim; Priscilla's grave.

Excluded: "old-fashioned lawman with a strict no-nonsense work ethic", "remaining fair to the law", "clearly a skilled
shootist", "keeps cool under the intense pressure", "a grudge against government agents" (wiki interpretation; the
transcripts are quoted instead); the jurisdiction "inconsistencies" and the theory that he took on extra duties for
lack of a sheriff (wiki trivia, analysis); the causes of the yellow beard (alcohol, chewing tobacco, blond hair: wiki
"may be"); the FR wiki "il n'a pas l'air de comprendre la modernité", "il semble en réalité détester cette ville" and
"il a sans doute refusé de s'allier à Edgar Ross" (interpretation, speculation); the FR wiki "methods diablement
efficaces mais très archaïques" (opinion); the FR wiki's allies list naming Seth and Irish (no exchange between them
and Johnson in any transcript: the entries below say so); Baxter Deaton's rumors as facts (gossip; Baxter admits he
makes most of it up); Mel Thaxton's sexual rumor (gossip, not repeated); the wiki trivia that "Jake" says Johnson is not the man he used to be (the linked Jake is the guide of "Exodus in America", whose transcript has no such line); "Be careful with that thing" (a line Colin
Nissan quotes in his Paris Review piece; not in any transcript).
"""


